  "details": "client version w_2019.3.2.p4\nI've found out that I get stuck in a login loop, that is--unable to log in VRChat, click Okay, then client repeats logging in indefinitely-- when the client gets an invalid DNS response to ns.exitgames.com.\nLog entry:\n======\n2020.03.01 09:55:15 Error      -  Connect() to 'ns.exitgames.com' (InterNetwork) failed: System.Net.Sockets.SocketException: The requested address is not valid in its context.\n  at System.Net.Sockets.Socket.Connect (System.Net.EndPoint remoteEP, Boolean requireSocketPolicy) [0x00000] in <filename unknown>:0 \n  at System.Net.Sockets.Socket.Connect (System.Net.EndPoint remoteEP) [0x00000] in <filename unknown>:0 \n  at System.Net.Sockets.Socket.Connect (System.Net.IPAddress address, Int32 port) [0x00000] in <filename unknown>:0 \n  at ExitGames.Client.Photon.SocketUdp.DnsAndConnect () [0x00000] in <filename unknown>:0 \n2020.03.01 09:55:15 Log        -  [NetworkManager] OnDisconnected: ExceptionOnConnect\n2020.03.01 09:55:15 Error      -  [VRCFlowNetworkManager] {{ NameServerAddress: 'ns.exitgames.com:5058', MasterServerAddress: '', GameServerAddress: '', Code: 'ExceptionOnConnect', State: 'Disconnected', Time: '0' }}\n2020.03.01 09:55:15 Log        -  [VRCFlowNetworkManager] Disconnected: ExceptionOnConnect with Reason: \n2020.03.01 09:55:15 Log        -  [VRCFlowManagerVRC] Resetting game flow because \"Failed to connect to VRChat.\": [ShowUI]\n======\nDNS resolution:\nPS C:\\Users\\dingo> Resolve-DnsName ns.exitgames.com\nName                                           Type   TTL   Section    IPAddress\n----                                           ----   ---   -------    ---------\nns.exitgames.com                               AAAA   2     Answer     ::\nns.exitgames.com                               A      2     Answer     0.0.0.0\n=====\nMitigation is to either create a hostsfile entry for ns.exitgames.com or in my case, whitelist ns.exitgames.com on DNS filtering software like pihole in my case.",
